  "question": {
    "text": "A beaker of height&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>H</mi></math> is made up of a material whose coefficient of linear thermal expansion is <math> <mrow> <mn>3</mn> <mi>α</mi> </mrow> </math>. It is filled up to the brim by a liquid whose coefficient of volume expansion is <math> <mrow> <mn>3</mn> <mi>α</mi> </mrow> </math>. If now the beaker along with its contents is uniformly heated through a small temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math>, the level of liquid will reduce by (Given, <math> <mrow> <mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>≪</mo><mn>1</mn> </mrow> </math>)"
